1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,384
A Signal Group combines a few signals into one reading, with labels you choose,

2
00:00:04,404 --> 00:00:06,209
such as Bullish or Bearish.

3
00:00:06,677 --> 00:00:09,537
Open Angstrom Lattice, then Signal Groups.

4
00:00:09,587 --> 00:00:12,276
On the left is every signal you can use.

5
00:00:15,428 --> 00:00:19,184
Signals come in six families, each answering one question.

6
00:00:19,234 --> 00:00:21,518
Trend asks: which way is it going?

7
00:00:21,568 --> 00:00:23,553
The icons filter the list.

8
00:00:24,015 --> 00:00:25,958
Tap plus to add a signal.

9
00:00:26,008 --> 00:00:27,566
Trend direction.

10
00:00:27,616 --> 00:00:31,671
Then moving averages, choosing the fifty and two-hundred day version.

11
00:00:31,721 --> 00:00:33,344
And the MACD line.

12
00:00:34,547 --> 00:00:39,007
Each signal can add to the score, act as a condition, or just give context.

13
00:00:39,057 --> 00:00:43,688
Here all three add to one score, from minus one hundred to plus one hundred.

14
00:00:44,149 --> 00:00:46,433
Rules turn the score into labels.

15
00:00:46,483 --> 00:00:50,943
Bullish when the score is thirty or more. Bearish when it's minus thirty or less.

16
00:00:50,993 --> 00:00:52,637
Otherwise, Neutral.

17
00:00:53,879 --> 00:00:56,248
Give it a name, My Trend, and save it.

18
00:01:01,380 --> 00:01:06,395
My Trend now works anywhere a Group can be used: in Signal Sets, scans and funnels.
